#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:51
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:53
msgid ""
"This default preset for cssnano only includes transforms that make no "
"assumptions about your CSS other than what is passed in. In previous "
"iterations of cssnano, assumptions were made about your CSS which caused "
"output to look different in certain use cases, but not others. These "
"transforms have been moved from the defaults to other presets, to make "
"this preset require only minimal configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:61
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:63
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:65
msgid ""
"Note that this preset comes bundled with cssnano _by default_, so you "
"don't need to install it separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:67
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:69
msgid ""
"If you would like to use the default configuration, then you don't need "
"to add anything to your `package.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:71
msgid ""
"But should you wish to customise this, you can pass an array with the "
"second parameter as the options object to use. For example, to remove all"
" comments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:85
msgid ""
"Depending on your usage, the JSON configuration might not work for you, "
"such as in cases where you would like to use options with customisable "
"function parameters. For this use case, we recommend a "
"`cssnano.config.js` at the same location as your `package.json`. You can "
"then load a preset and export it with your custom parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssnano-preset-default_README.md:97
msgid ""
"Note that you may wish to publish your own preset to npm for reusability,"
" should it differ a lot from this one. This is highly encouraged!"
msgstr ""

